ter  municipal and corporate buildings  ladies and gentlemen pervert cold let's  wreck his world there is an art to  accomplishing your goals without being  noticed but if you prefer to stand tall  and carry a big stick  no major character questions your  tactics least of all Marcus himself you  are free to steal cars Rob the innocent  and infiltrate using brute force over  covert hacks provided you're good at  running from the police and watchdog  twos tongue-in-cheek world you're never  forced to confront the moral  consequences of your actions beyond  watching witnesses flee a crime scene  San Francisco and other Bay Area cities  and watchdogs to look and feel like  they're real counterparts but there is a  noticeable lack of traffic on sidewalks  and city streets this affords you fewer  opportunities to create chaos as a  result but the modestly populated roads  do make it easy to cruise around the bay  driving feels marginally better than the  last game with motorcycles offering the  most control and utility  there's a wonderful mix of urban variety  and natural beauty on the map and the  steep hills of San Francisco offer  plenty of opportunities for  death-defying stunts you can distract  yourself from the daunting task of  hacking the world by racing motocross  bikes go-karts and drones you can also  work on your selfie game and drive for a  ride-sharing service to earn extra cash  and attract new dedsec followers which  in turn allows you to unlock new hacking  abilities and purchase new weapons  though you are encouraged to shoot for a  specific playstyle you'll have no  problem if you diversify your skill sets  in fact the best moments in watchdogs 2  are when it presents open-ended  challenges that inspire you to mix and  match between hacking and armed combat  part of the reason watchdogs too can  allow you to be sneaky or explosive at a  moment's notice is that it's AI has a  few screws loose you aren't given the  chance to hide bodies which makes  stealth feel like a non option but this  is accounted for by easily distracted  NPCs with a simple command you can  distract or overwhelm enemies through  their smartphone even when they know  something sketchy is afoot then knock  them out before they can call for help  you can drive forklifts and scissor  lifts through crowds but no one seems to  bothered by the inconvenience with fast  and loose rules watchdogs too won't win  any points for realism but it does allow  you room to be the creative action hero  you apparently are there is a lot of joy  defined in playing watchdogs to solo but  multiplayer  when it works shouldn't be ignored there  are emergent PvP events that allow you  to hack or hunt down other players and  special missions were you and a partner  can infiltrate networks and private  property together we can imagine how a  full server of players has the potential  to make you feel connected to the world  and part of a larger community of  hackers we just can't test that theory  until the game is in the hands of more  people  watchdogs to is definitely an enjoyable  game but it remains to be seen if it can  seamlessly marry single and multiplayer  content without a hitch  Marcus we're on the news already
 

